{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l224gt0q","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"simple-harmonic-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"simple-harmonic-motion","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-small-block-is-connected-to-one-end-of-a-massless-sprin-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-fxsn4oczfaawk3e3","content":"<p>A small block is connected to one end of a massless spring of un-stretched length 4.9 m. The other end of the spring (see the figure) is fixed. The system lies on a horizontal frictionless surface. The block is stretched by 0.2 m and released from rest at t = 0. It then executes simple harmonic motion with angular frequency <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>/3) rad/s. Simultaneously, at t = 0, a small pebble is projected with speed v from point P at an angle of 45<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> as shown in the figure. Point O is at a horizontal distance of 10 m from O. If the pebble hits the block at t = 1 s, the value of v is (take g = 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Simple Harmonic Motion Question 21 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-88fd-9e81392d343f/6c4edbf0-bf02-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24krui8.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l24krui7/bbec5170-14b2-434b-8